      "id": 1,
      "claim": "In fantasy and mythological lore a \"true name\" is a magical identifier that represents the essence of a being.",
      "evidence": "Sources such as Ursula K. Le Guin’s Earthsea series, Dungeons & Dragons rules, and folklore (e.g., Rumpelstiltskin) describe true names as the metaphysical core of a creature.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "claim": "Knowing a being’s true name acts as a key that lets a caster direct magical energy specifically at that being, enabling the caster to affect the target with spells.",
      "evidence": "In Earthsea, a wizard must know a person’s true name to cast any spell that influences that person; D&D’s \"Name of Power\" mechanics similarly require the true name to bind or affect a creature.",
      "weight": 0.35,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "Because the true name is the conduit for magical influence, it grants the ability to cast any spell on the person whose true name is known.",
      "evidence": "The key function of the true name is to bypass normal protections and allow the caster to apply any magical effect—healing, curses, compulsion, fireball, etc.—to the target.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "Option E (“You can use a person's true name to cast spells on them”) best captures this broad capability, whereas the other options describe specific subsets (A, D, F, B) or a non‑magical use (C).",
      "evidence": "Casting spells is the superset of cursing, forcing obedience, controlling, or reflecting spells; therefore the most accurate answer is the general ability to cast spells.",
      "weight": 0.10,
      "depends_on": [3]
    }
  ],
  "answer": "E",
  "confidence": 0.94,
  "considered": [
    {
      "answer": "D",
      "reason_rejected": "Forcing obedience is only one possible spell effect; the true name’s primary description is the general ability to cast spells, not a single specific outcome."
    },
    {
      "answer": "F",
      "reason_rejected": "\"Control\" is a vague subset of magical influence and does not encompass the full range of spell types enabled by a true name."
    },
    {
      "answer": "A",
      "reason_rejected": "Cursing is just one type of spell; the true name is not limited to curses."
    },
